Use the Stable Haskell GHC's `-fully-static` for `executable-static`.

`executable-static: True` reaches Cabal as `withFullyStaticExe`, and
`modules/cabal-project.nix` sets it in `package *` for every musl host,
meaning "every executable should be statically linked" -- what haskell.nix's
v1 builder does for musl with `--ghc-option=-optl=-static`.

The stable-haskell/merge Cabal (3.19) spells that the upstream way,
`ghcOptLinkOptions = ["-static"]` (`-optl-static`), which is right for
upstream GHC.  A Stable Haskell GHC has a flag that says exactly this,
`-fully-static` ("Link all libraries statically [...] This includes external
libraries, Haskell libraries, as well as libc"), and ghc914-sh musl
executables (iserv-proxy-interpreter's reference to musl's hidden
`__aio_close`, the cabal-simple "statically linked" check) need it.

Ask the compiler instead of assuming: the fork brands its `ghc --info` with
`("Edition","Stable Haskell")` and upstream emits no such field (haskell.nix
relies on the same discriminator in `lib/dummy-ghc.nix`).  Other compilers
keep the merge's `-optl-static`.

(Earlier versions of this patch replaced the older fork's `-static-external`,
which deliberately left libc dynamic and which upstream GHC rejects.  The
merge no longer emits it.)

diff --git a/src/Distribution/Simple/GHC/Build/Link.hs b/src/Distribution/Simple/GHC/Build/Link.hs
index 99f9135eb..c1e523943 100644
--- a/src/Distribution/Simple/GHC/Build/Link.hs
+++ b/src/Distribution/Simple/GHC/Build/Link.hs
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@ import Prelude ()
 import Control.Monad
 import Control.Monad.IO.Class
 import qualified Data.ByteString.Lazy.Char8 as BS
+import qualified Data.Map as Map
 import qualified Data.Set as Set
 import qualified Data.Text as Text
 import Distribution.Backpack
@@ -120,13 +121,28 @@ linkOrLoadComponent
         | src <- extraSources
         ]
 
+      -- `withFullyStaticExe` is `executable-static: True`.  A Stable Haskell
+      -- GHC has a `-fully-static` flag for that, which also links its own
+      -- runtime dependencies statically; upstream GHC does not, and only
+      -- gets the linker's `-static`.  The fork brands its `ghc --info` with
+      -- `Edition`, and upstream emits no such field.
+      ghcHasFullyStatic =
+        Map.lookup "Edition" (compilerProperties (compiler lbi))
+          == Just "Stable Haskell"
+
       -- TODO: Shouldn't we use withStaticLib for libraries and something else
       -- for foreign libs in the three cases where we use `withFullyStaticExe` below?
       linkerOpts rpaths =
         mempty
-          { ghcOptLinkOptions =
+          { ghcOptExtraDefault =
+              [ "-fully-static"
+              | withFullyStaticExe lbi
+              , ghcHasFullyStatic
+              ]
+          , ghcOptLinkOptions =
               [ "-static"
               | withFullyStaticExe lbi
+              , not ghcHasFullyStatic
               ]
                 -- Pass extra `ld-options` given
                 -- through to GHC's linker.
